-- title:
--   Bounded exponent of vertex stabilisers on the Bruhat–Tits tree
-- statement:
--   Let $R_0$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain with the `IsDiscreteValuationRing` property) whose residue field is finite, and let $K_0$ be a field equipped with an $R_0$-algebra structure making it a fraction field of $R_0$. Write $\mathrm{Vertex}\,R_0\,K_0$ for the set of homothety classes of full $R_0$-lattices in $K_0^2 = (\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to K_0)$, and let `BruhatTits.tree R₀ K₀` be the simple graph on these classes generated by the relation `VertRel`, which holds of two classes when they admit full-lattice representatives $L, L'$ satisfying `AdjacentLattice L L'`. Let $\Delta$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$, acting on the vertices. Assume that for every dart $d$ of the tree (an ordered pair of adjacent vertices) the stabiliser of $d$ in $\Delta$ is finite, and that the orbit quotient $\mathrm{Quot\,Vert}\,\Delta\,(\mathrm{Vertex}\,R_0\,K_0)$, i.e. the quotient of the vertex set by the $\Delta$-orbit relation, is finite. Then there exists a natural number $m > 0$ such that for every vertex $w$ and every $\gamma \in \Delta$ with $\gamma \cdot w = w$ one has $\gamma^m = 1$ in $\Delta$.
--
--   This is the statement that a cocompact tree lattice with finite dart stabilisers has vertex stabilisers of bounded exponent, for the action of a subgroup of $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ on the Bruhat–Tits tree of a local discrete valuation ring. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where it feeds into [`CerednikDrinfeld.BruhatTits.exists_pos_forall_isOfFinOrder_pow_eq_one`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.BruhatTits.exists_pos_forall_isOfFinOrder_pow_eq_one), the passage from an arbitrary character of $\Delta$ to a power of it that is trivial on all vertex stabilisers.
